<title>POLAND: Poland sets minimum sugar price at 1.33 zlotys/kg.</title>
<headline>Poland sets minimum sugar price at 1.33 zlotys/kg.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish government set the minimum sugar wholesale price for 1996/97 at 1.33 zlotys/kg and the white sugar domestic production quota for the period at 1.63 million tonnes, it said in a statement.  </p>
<p>In the 1995/96 season, which runs from October 1, 1995 to September 30, 1996, the minimum price was 1.16 zlotys/kg.</p>
<p>On Tuesday the government also set the 1997/98 domestic production quota at 1.63 million tonnes, up from 1.50 million tonnes in the 1996/97 season.</p>
<p>It also set the subsidised export quota for 1997/98 at 113,700 tonnes, down from 122,900 tonnes in 1996/97 in line with international trade agreements, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
